---
// About page: what Buy Risk is, the buy-risk thesis, and the full research and
// dataset citation lists (rendered from src/data/citations).
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Sources from "../components/Sources.astro";
import { STUDIES, DATASETS } from "../data/citations";

const allStudyIds = Object.keys(STUDIES);
const allDatasetIds = Object.keys(DATASETS);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="What Buy Risk is, who it's for, and the principles behind the way we teach investing."
>
  <section class="container about">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Financial literacy is for everyone, but it can be counterintuitive.</h1>

      <p>
        <strong>Buy Risk</strong> exists because most investing content is
        either trying to sell you something or assumes you already have an MBA.
        We think the core ideas are genuinely learnable by anyone willing to
        spend an afternoon with them, and that they're far more simple and
        interesting than the hype makes them sound.
      </p>

      <h2>What we believe</h2>
      <p>
        The name is our thesis. Every real investment return is compensation for
        bearing some form of risk. You don't earn a premium by being clever; you
        earn it by holding uncertainty, and by doing it patiently, cheaply, and
        in diversified form.
      </p>

      <h2>How we teach</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Plain language first.</strong> If a concept needs jargon, we
          define it before we use it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Show, don't just tell.</strong> Our <a href="/tools">tools</a>
          let you manipulate the variables yourself, because intuition comes
          from playing, not reading.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Evidence over stories.</strong> We lean on the boring,
          well-supported findings of finance (diversification, compounding, and
          the cost of fees), not hot tips.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>An important note</h2>
      <p>
        Everything on Buy Risk is educational. It is not personalized financial
        advice, and we don't know your situation. Use it to understand how
        investing works, then make your own decisions, or talk to a licensed
        professional who can account for your specific circumstances.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you do want personal guidance, the same idea that runs through this
        site applies to the advice itself: understand what you're paying and what
        you get for it. Advisors charge in different ways (a flat or hourly fee, a
        percentage of your assets, or commissions on products), and any of them can
        be worth it as long as the cost is clear to you. A fee-only, advice-only
        advisor is one transparent, low-conflict place to start; directories like
        the <a
          href="https://adviceonlynetwork.com/#advisors"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Advice-Only Network</a> list them.
      </p>

      <p>
        Ready to dig in? Jump straight to the
        <a href="/tools/compound-growth">compound growth explorer</a>, or browse
        the full <a href="/tools">Portfolio Playground</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, corrections, or an idea for a tool? Email us at
        <a href="mailto:buyriskHQ@gmail.com">buyriskHQ@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Author bio slots in here when ready. Northwestern faculty; frame as the
      project's scholarship / academic-service note. */}

  <Sources
    studies={allStudyIds}
    datasets={allDatasetIds}
    grouped
    title="Data & research"
    intro="Buy Risk is built on the primary sources of evidence-based finance. Every figure on the site traces back to peer-reviewed research or a public dataset; the works below anchor the tools, grouped by theme."
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>
